# Project docs: CLAUDE.md is the single source

**CLAUDE.md** at the repo root is the canonical project guidance. It is used by:

- **Claude Code** (claude.ai/code) when you work in this repo there
- **Cursor** in this workspace (via this rule and workspace rules)

To keep both in sync:

- **Do not** create a separate Cursor-only doc (e.g. AGENTS.md or another rule) that duplicates architecture, commands, or conventions from CLAUDE.md.
- **Do** update **CLAUDE.md** whenever you change project documentation: architecture, commands, CLI options, key types, testing setup, or Node/ESM details. That way Claude Code and Cursor always see the same guidance.

When adding or changing features, update CLAUDE.md as part of the change so the two environments stay aligned.
